    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "34 Stratford Haven is a two-bedroom mid-terrace townhouse located within this well-established and highly regarded development of fewer than 60 homes.  The property offers a wonderful opportunity to acquire a property in one of Dublin 6’s most sought-after locations. With a private rear garden, designated parking and ample visitor parking, this charming townhouse provides a superb foundation for creating a stylish and contemporary home.\r\n\r\nThe property is ideally suited to a range of purchasers, including first-time buyers, downsizers and investors, while its well-proportioned accommodation and excellent location will undoubtedly appeal to those seeking a home with genuine potential.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is well laid out, on entering, there is a welcoming entrance hallway with guest WC and access to the living room. The living room features useful understairs storage and opens through to the kitchen/dining area, which in turn has patio doors leading directly to the rear garden.\r\nUpstairs, there are two particularly spacious double bedrooms, both benefiting from built-in wardrobes, together with a family bathroom.\r\n\r\nTo the rear is a private, low-maintenance townhouse garden, predominantly paved and incorporating a small concrete block shed, providing useful additional storage.\r\n\r\nRequiring some modernisation, the property offers the discerning purchaser an exciting opportunity to introduce their own style and finishes, creating a sophisticated home in an enviable Rathgar setting.\r\n\r\nThe location is a major attraction, with Rathgar and the surrounding areas offering an excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities. There are also a number of highly regarded schools in the surrounding area, while the property is well positioned for access to Dublin city centre and the many amenities of Dublin 6."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor:\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall: Step in from the porch area to a door leading to the living room and stairs to the first floor.\r\n\r\nGuest W.C.: Fully tiled walls and floor with two piece white suite and window for natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 6.19m (max) x 3.9m (max) With bay window and marble surround open fireplace.  Understairs storage and door to:\r\n\r\nKitchen: 3.9m x 2.82m  Eye and floor level kitchen units with tall fridge freezer, washing machine, dryer, slimline dishwasher and electric cooker.  Tiled floor and splashback.  Patio doors to garden.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor:\r\n\r\nLanding: Spacious landing with access to the attic via pull-down stairs.\r\n\r\nFront Bedroom: 3.9m (max) x 3.55m With carpet, wardrobes and bay window.\r\n\r\nRear Bedroom: 3.3m x 2.75m With carpet and double wardrobes.  \r\n\r\nBathroom: 2.16m x 1.64m.  With three piece white suite. Fully tiled walls and floor.  Hotpress.  Velux window for natural light and ventilation."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Approx. 68 sq.m. \r\nElectric heating \r\nDouble glazed windows\r\nDesignated car space and ample visitor parking\r\nLovely communal garden to the front and private townhouse garden to the rear\r\nNo onward chain\r\nBER Cert: C\r\nBER No: 119720142\r\nService charge: €1,350 per annum\r\nLocated in the centre of Rathgar Village close to all local amenities and within easy access of the city centre"
      },
      {
